      "writtenOn": "2024-05-03T17:26:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e If you enabled the low memory allocator before, you will get it after.\n\nApologies at dragging this out, but the wording in the commit message has me a little confused.\n\nI understand that if a target set `MALLOC_SVELTE :\u003d true` before, that behavior will remain the same.  But if a target didn\u0027t set `MALLOC_SVELTE` at all before, what were they getting?  The \"Change this so that the default is the regular allocator\" wording has me concerned that before they were getting the equivalent of `MALLOC_SVELTE :\u003d true`, and after this change they would get the equivalent of `MALLOC_SVELTE :\u003d false`.\n\nIf that\u0027s the case, I don\u0027t oppose this change in default behavior.  I just want to make sure teams potentially impacted by it are in the loop.\n\nThanks!",
      "parentUuid": "4fdb952f_37e0d4e8",
